+        """``max_turns`` reaches the CLI at every value the caller can set.
+
+        The CLI declares ``--max-turns <turns>`` with a parser that only
+        rejects NaN, and documents it as "early exit the conversation after
+        the specified number of turns" -- so 0 means zero turns, not "no
+        limit". Dropping it on a falsy check would hand a caller who asked
